  "notes": "Public Beta 13 - P23 'Continuation without destruction': verified work now survives the turn boundary. A continuation turn carries a pinned ARTIFACT STATE block re-read from disk, a user claim that contradicts verified evidence gets reproduced before anything is rewritten, and shrinking rewrites that drop definitions are held once with the removals named. Endings are loud and honest: every turn ends with one stated reason, a round is never 'dry' while its own checks still fail, error rounds are charged only against a provider-health probe, and a transient outage parks and resumes instead of giving up. Tool results stopped lying: python registry saves say where they landed, a killed command reports what it did before the deadline, and directory tools teach instead of emitting OS jargon. Plus live (no longer boot-frozen) summarization-priority, GUI steering that no longer reads as failure, and two invalid installer-config keys that blocked builds outright.",
